    <p>Remodeling has always run on word of mouth, and in a town Hartselle's size it feels like enough — everybody's last addition was somebody's cousin's crew. But the town is growing precisely because of people your referral network doesn't reach. The family relocating from Huntsville for the lower home prices and the Hartselle City Schools has no builder to ask, because they don't know anyone here yet — so they search. The out-of-state buyer who just closed on an older home to renovate it is typing "Hartselle remodel contractor" into Google, not calling a neighbor they don't have. Those transplants are the growth, and they never touch your referral chain, which is exactly <a href="/articles/why-word-of-mouth-isnt-enough/">the ceiling word of mouth hits</a> the moment a town draws people faster than your reputation can travel. A real page is the only thing that puts you in front of them.</p>

